   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an\napplication for a real property tax exemption from Ray of Hope, Inc.",
    "basePrintNo": "S10203",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10203-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10203\n\nSPONSOR: BYNOE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption from Ray of\nHope, Inc.\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the County of Nassau Assessor to accept from the Ray of Hope,\nInc. an application for exemption from real property taxes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill authorizes the assessor of the county of nassau to\naccept from Ray of Hope Inc., located at 760 St. Lukes Pl, Baldwin, NY\n11510, an application for exemption from real property taxes pursuant to\nsection 420a of the real property tax law. Upon approval by the nassau\ncounty legislature, the assessor may make appropriate correction to the\nsubject rolls.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would provide Ray of Hope, Inc. with an exemption from\nreal property taxes pursuant to Section 420-a of the Real Property Tax\nLaw. Ray of Hope, Inc. is a not-for-profit place for worship in the\nHamlet of Baldwin. This legislation will provide for the Nassau County\nAssessor's Office to correct this error and grant their exemption, and\ntherefore issue a refund for taxes paid.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
